SRR22963633	PRJNA917767	SRP415646	SAMN32547031	SRX18920257	Homo sapiens	final_rep2	final_rep2	Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6914874: final_rep2 Homo sapiens OTHER	OTHER	GENOMIC	other	SINGLE	ILLUMINA	Illumina NovaSeq 6000	Genomic DNA was extracted from each cell population using a QIAGEN Blood Maxi kit (for GFP low cells) or QIAGEN Blood Midi kit (for GFP high cells). sgRNAs sequences were amplified from genomic DNA samples using the Herculase II Fusion DNA Polymerase (Agilent Technologies) in two PCR steps as follows. In the first PCR, the genomic region containing sgRNAs were amplified from 130 µg total DNA using the following primers: Forward: 5'-AATGGACTATCATATGCTTACCGTAACTTGAAAGTATTTCG-3' Reverse: 5'-CTTTAGTTTGTATGTCTGTTGCTATTATGTCTACTATTCTTTCC-3'. In total, 13 PCR reactions were performed in parallel, with 10 µg genomic DNA in each reaction using Herculase II Fusion DNA Polymerase (Agilent) for 18 cycles and the resulting PCR products were combined. In the second step PCR, 5 µl of first PCR product was used in a 100 µl reaction volume and 24 PCR cycles was used. The primers used for the second PCR include stagger sequences of variable lengths and a 6bp barcode for multiplexing of different biological samples. The 2nd step PCR primers were used as the following: Forward: 5'-AATGATACGGCGACCACCGAGATCTACACTCTTTCCCTACACGACGCTCTTCCGATCT (1-9bp variable length sequence)-(6bp barcode)tcttgtggaaaggacgaaacaccg-3' Reverse: 5'-CAAGCAGAAGACGGCATACGAGATGTGACTGGAGTTCAGACGTGTGCTCTTCCGATCT tctactattctttcccctgcactgt-3'. sgRNAs amplified from genomic DNA	28101265	1545569575	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR229/033/SRR22963633/SRR22963633.fastq.gz	a96a849d1e93f6a972ade9f5b3d71eda	557385347
